         <div type="translation" resp="part:vito">
             <p>Gift of the <foreign>upāsaka</foreign> Bodhigutta, the son of the notable Viḍanāgila.</p>
         </div>
         <div type="bibliography">
            <p>The reunion of both elements is due to Robert Arlt. The fragment bearing <bibl><ptr target="bib:Nakanishi+Hinuber2014_01"/><citedRange unit="page">110</citedRange><citedRange unit="section">V.2</citedRange><citedRange unit="item">4</citedRange></bibl> fits perfectly in the top right corner of the slab bearing <bibl><ptr target="bib:Nakanishi+Hinuber2014_01"/><citedRange unit="page">110</citedRange><citedRange unit="section">V.2</citedRange><citedRange unit="item">3</citedRange></bibl>. The text is closely related to <bibl><ptr target="bib:Nakanishi+Hinuber2014_01"/><citedRange unit="page">110</citedRange><citedRange unit="section">V.2</citedRange><citedRange unit="item">1</citedRange></bibl>, in part misread by <bibl><ptr target="bib:Nakanishi+Hinuber2014_01"/></bibl>, which further supports this juncture.</p>
            <p>This edition, based on photographs, by Vincent Tournier. Encoded in XML by Fu Fan in July 2025.</p>
